\";\r\n  $result = mysqli_query($connection, $sql);\r\n  if ($result->num_rows() > 0) {\r\n    echo \'Row added successfully.\';\r\n  }\r\n;\r\n  $sql2 = \"SELECT * FROM table_name;\";\r\n  $result2 = mysqli_query($connection, $sql2);\r\n\r\n  if ($result2->num_rows() > 0) {\r\n    echo \'Rows selected from the table.\';\r\n  }\r\n;\r\n?>\";success|s:40:\"Generated successfully. Cost: 1 credits.\";'),('ci_session:242903ce6aa2106ddd4ed5eea5c5f0ac','::1',4294967295,_binary '__ci_last_regenerate|i:1764620949;_ci_previous_url|s:24:\"https://localhost/gemini\";isLoggedIn|b:1;userId|i:1;userEmail|s:23:\"nehemiahobati@gmail.com\";username|s:8:\"nehemiah\";is_admin|b:1;member_since|O:21:\"CodeIgniter\\I18n\\Time\":6:{s:4:\"date\";s:26:\"2025-11-20 22:30:57.000000\";s:13:\"timezone_type\";i:3;s:8:\"timezone\";s:14:\"Africa/Nairobi\";s:11:\"\0*\0timezone\";O:12:\"DateTimeZone\":2:{s:13:\"timezone_type\";i:3;s:8:\"timezone\";s:14:\"Africa/Nairobi\";}s:9:\"\0*\0locale\";s:2:\"en\";s:17:\"\0*\0toStringFormat\";s:19:\"yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss\";}'),('ci_session:248bb6c20f1a96dd9844d83bd8e72e69','::1',4294967295,_binary '__ci_last_regenerate|i:1764604352;_ci_previous_url|s:24:\"https://localhost/gemini\";isLoggedIn|b:1;userId|i:1;userEmail|s:23:\"nehemiahobati@gmail.com\";username|s:8:\"nehemiah\";is_admin|b:1;member_since|O:21:\"CodeIgniter\\I18n\\Time\":6:{s:4:\"date\";s:26:\"2025-11-20 22:30:57.000000\";s:13:\"timezone_type\";i:3;s:8:\"timezone\";s:14:\"Africa/Nairobi\";s:11:\"\0*\0timezone\";O:12:\"DateTimeZone\":2:{s:13:\"timezone_type\";i:3;s:8:\"timezone\";s:14:\"Africa/Nairobi\";}s:9:\"\0*\0locale\";s:2:\"en\";s:17:\"\0*\0toStringFormat\";s:19:\"yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss\";}__ci_vars|a:0:{}'),('ci_session:2648cc834103310f126514fba60df7bf','::1',4294967295,_binary '__ci_last_regenerate|i:1764608595;_ci_previous_url|s:18:\"https://localhost/\";isLoggedIn|b:1;userId|i:1;userEmail|s:23:\"nehemiahobati@gmail.com\";username|s:8:\"nehemiah\";is_admin|b:1;member_since|O:21:\"CodeIgniter\\I18n\\Time\":6:{s:4:\"date\";s:26:\"2025-11-20 22:30:57.000000\";s:13:\"timezone_type\";i:3;s:8:\"timezone\";s:14:\"Africa/Nairobi\";s:11:\"\0*\0timezone\";O:12:\"DateTimeZone\":2:{s:13:\"timezone_type\";i:3;s:8:\"timezone\";s:14:\"Africa/Nairobi\";}s:9:\"\0*\0locale\";s:2:\"en\";s:17:\"\0*\0toStringFormat\";s:19:\"yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss\";}__ci_vars|a:0:{}'),('ci_session:2a36f5847f9b7ca3e8aa0c0cf8d10d2c','::1',4294967295,_binary '__ci_last_regenerate|i:1764713780;_ci_previous_url|s:24:\"https://localhost/gemini\";isLoggedIn|b:1;userId|i:1;userEmail|s:23:\"nehemiahobati@gmail.com\";username|s:8:\"nehemiah\";is_admin|b:1;member_since|O:21:\"CodeIgniter\\I18n\\Time\":6:{s:4:\"date\";s:26:\"2025-11-20 22:30:57.000000\";s:13:\"timezone_type\";i:3;s:8:\"timezone\";s:14:\"Africa/Nairobi\";s:11:\"\0*\0timezone\";O:12:\"DateTimeZone\":2:{s:13:\"timezone_type\";i:3;s:8:\"timezone\";s:14:\"Africa/Nairobi\";}s:9:\"\0*\0locale\";s:2:\"en\";s:17:\"\0*\0toStringFormat\";s:19:\"yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss\";}success|s:18:\"KSH 1.10 deducted.\";__ci_vars|a:4:{s:7:\"success\";s:3:\"old\";s:13:\"_ci_old_input\";s:3:\"old\";s:6:\"result\";s:3:\"old\";s:10:\"raw_result\";s:3:\"old\";}_ci_old_input|a:2:{s:3:\"get\";a:0:{}s:4:\"post\";a:3:{s:8:\"model_id\";s:16:\"gemini-2.0-flash\";s:15:\"generation_type\";s:4:\"text\";s:6:\"prompt\";s:23:\"<p>sample php code.</p>\";}}result|s:2981:\"<p>PHP (Hypertext Preprocessor) is a widely-used open-source scripting language especially suited for web development and can be embedded into HTML. Here are some sample code snippets to illustrate its basic functionalities.</p>\n<h3>1. Hello, World!</h3>\n<p>This is the most basic PHP script, which outputs a simple text string.</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-php\">&lt;?php\n  echo \"Hello, World!\";\n?&gt;</code></pre>\n<p>You can also embed PHP within an HTML document.</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;title&gt;PHP Test&lt;/title&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;p&gt;&lt;?php echo \"Hello, World!\"; ?&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;</code></pre>\n<h3>2. Working with Variables and Arrays</h3>\n<p>PHP variables are declared with a dollar sign (<code>$</code>). Here\'s an example of using variables and a simple loop to iterate through an array.</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-php\">&lt;?php\n  $greeting = \"Welcome to our fruit stand!\";\n  $fruits = [\"Apple\", \"Banana\", \"Orange\"];\n\n  echo \"&lt;h1&gt;\" . $greeting . \"&lt;/h1&gt;\";\n\n  echo \"&lt;ul&gt;\";\n  foreach ($fruits as $fruit) {\n    echo \"&lt;li&gt;\" . $fruit . \"&lt;/li&gt;\";\n  }\n  echo \"&lt;/ul&gt;\";\n?&gt;</code></pre>\n<h3>3. Handling Form Submissions</h3>\n<p>PHP is commonly used to process data submitted from HTML forms.</p>\n<p><strong>HTML Form (<code>index.html</code>)</strong></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;title&gt;PHP Form&lt;/title&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;form action=\"welcome.php\" method=\"post\"&gt;\n    Name: &lt;input type=\"text\" name=\"name\"&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n    E-mail: &lt;input type=\"text\" name=\"email\"&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n    &lt;input type=\"submit\"&gt;\n  &lt;/form&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;</code></pre>\n<p><strong>PHP Script (<code>welcome.php</code>)</strong></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-php\">&lt;?php\n  if ($_SERVER[\"REQUEST_METHOD\"] == \"POST\") {\n    $name = htmlspecialchars($_POST[\'name\']);\n    $email = htmlspecialchars($_POST[\'email\']);\n    echo \"Welcome, \" . $name . \"!&lt;br&gt;\";\n    echo \"Your email address is: \" . $email;\n  }\n?&gt;</code></pre>\n<p>In this example, the HTML form sends the data to <code>welcome.php</code> using the POST method. The PHP script then accesses this data using the <code>$_POST</code> superglobal array.</p>\n<h3>4. Simple Calculator using Functions</h3>\n<p>This example demonstrates defining and calling functions in PHP to perform a simple calculation.</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-php\">&lt;?php\n  function add($a, $b) {\n    return $a + $b;\n  }\n\n  function subtract($a, $b) {\n    return $a - $b;\n  }\n\n  $num1 = 20;\n  $num2 = 5;\n\n  echo \"Sum: \" . add($num1, $num2) . \"&lt;br&gt;\";\n  echo \"Difference: \" . subtract($num1, $num2);\n?&gt;</code></pre>\n<p>These examples cover some of the fundamental concepts of PHP programming. To run these examples, you will need a web server with PHP installed, such as XAMPP or WAMP.</p>\";raw_result|s:2383:\"PHP (Hypertext Preprocessor) is a widely-used open-source scripting language especially suited for web development and can be embedded into HTML. Here are some sample code snippets to illustrate its basic functionalities.\n\n### 1. Hello, World!\n\nThis is the most basic PHP script, which outputs a simple text string.\n\n```php\n<?php\n  echo \"Hello, World!\";\n?>\n```\n\nYou can also embed PHP within an HTML document.\n\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<head>\n  <title>PHP Test</title>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <p><?php echo \"Hello, World!\"; ?></p>\n</body>\n</html>\n```\n\n### 2. Working with Variables and Arrays\n\nPHP variables are declared with a dollar sign (`$`). Here\'s an example of using variables and a simple loop to iterate through an array.\n\n```php\n<?php\n  $greeting = \"Welcome to our fruit stand!\";\n  $fruits = [\"Apple\", \"Banana\", \"Orange\"];\n\n  echo \"<h1>\" . $greeting . \"</h1>\";\n\n  echo \"<ul>\";\n  foreach ($fruits as $fruit) {\n    echo \"<li>\" . $fruit . \"</li>\";\n  }\n  echo \"</ul>\";\n?>\n```\n\n### 3. Handling Form Submissions\n\nPHP is commonly used to process data submitted from HTML forms.\n\n**HTML Form (`index.html`)**\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<head>\n  <title>PHP Form</title>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <form action=\"welcome.php\" method=\"post\">\n    Name: <input type=\"text\" name=\"name\"><br>\n    E-mail: <input type=\"text\" name=\"email\"><br>\n    <input type=\"submit\">\n  </form>\n</body>\n</html>\n```\n\n**PHP Script (`welcome.php`)**\n```php\n<?php\n  if ($_SERVER[\"REQUEST_METHOD\"] == \"POST\") {\n    $name = htmlspecialchars($_POST[\'name\']);\n    $email = htmlspecialchars($_POST[\'email\']);\n    echo \"Welcome, \" . $name . \"!<br>\";\n    echo \"Your email address is: \" . $email;\n  }\n?>\n```\n\nIn this example, the HTML form sends the data to `welcome.php` using the POST method. The PHP script then accesses this data using the `$_POST` superglobal array.\n\n### 4. Simple Calculator using Functions\n\nThis example demonstrates defining and calling functions in PHP to perform a simple calculation.\n\n```php\n<?php\n  function add($a, $b) {\n    return $a + $b;\n  }\n\n  function subtract($a, $b) {\n    return $a - $b;\n  }\n\n  $num1 = 20;\n  $num2 = 5;\n\n  echo \"Sum: \" . add($num1, $num2) . \"<br>\";\n  echo \"Difference: \" . subtract($num1, $num2);\n?>\n```\n\nThese examples cover some of the fundamental concepts of PHP programming. To run these examples, you will need a web server with PHP installed, such as XAMPP or WAMP.\";'),('ci_session:2bd79ef5822dafcf94df8b5011848a51','::1',4294967295,_binary '__ci_last_regenerate|i:1764366065;_ci_previous_url|s:24:\"https://localhost/gemini\";isLoggedIn|b:1;userId|i:1;userEmail|s:23:\"nehemiahobati@gmail.com\";username|s:8:\"nehemiah\";is_admin|b:1;member_since|O:21:\"CodeIgniter\\I18n\\Time\":6:{s:4:\"date\";s:26:\"2025-11-20 22:30:57.000000\";s:13:\"timezone_type\";i:3;s:8:\"timezone\";s:14:\"Africa/Nairobi\";s:11:\"\0*\0timezone\";O:12:\"DateTimeZone\":2:{s:13:\"timezone_type\";i:3;s:8:\"timezone\";s:14:\"Africa/Nairobi\";}s:9:\"\0*\0locale\";s:2:\"en\";s:17:\"\0*\0toStringFormat\";s:19:\"yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss\";}__ci_vars|a:0:{}'),('ci_session:2c8434badbd91a4ee8f2691c9b24c701','::1',4294967295,_binary '__ci_last_regenerate|i:1764607873;_ci_previous_url|s:24:\"https://localhost/gemini\";isLoggedIn|b:1;userId|i:1;userEmail|s:23:\"nehemiahobati@gmail.com\";username|s:8:\"nehemiah\";is_admin|b:1;member_