}_ci_old_input|a:2:{s:3:\"get\";a:0:{}s:4:\"post\";a:3:{s:8:\"model_id\";s:16:\"gemini-2.0-flash\";s:15:\"generation_type\";s:4:\"text\";s:6:\"prompt\";s:52:\"<p>sample php code</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\";}}result|s:3374:\"<p>Of course, here are some PHP code samples ranging from basic to more advanced examples.</p>\n<h3>Basic &quot;Hello, World!&quot;</h3>\n<p>This is a classic example to demonstrate the basic syntax of PHP. It uses the <code>echo</code> statement to display a string of text.</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-php\">&lt;?php\n  echo \"Hello, World!\";\n?&gt;</code></pre>\n<h3>Variables</h3>\n<p>Variables are used to store information. In PHP, a variable starts with a <code>$</code> sign, followed by the name of the variable.</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-php\">&lt;?php\n  $greeting = \"Hello!\";\n  $month = 8;\n  $year = 2019;\n\n  echo $greeting; // Outputs: Hello!\n  echo $month;   // Outputs: 8\n  echo $year;    // Outputs: 2019\n?&gt;</code></pre>\n<h3>Conditional Statements (if-else)</h3>\n<p>Conditional statements are used to perform different actions based on different conditions.</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-php\">&lt;?php\n  $age = 20;\n\n  if ($age &gt;= 18) {\n    echo \"You are an adult.\";\n  } else {\n    echo \"You are a minor.\";\n  }\n?&gt;</code></pre>\n<h3>Loops</h3>\n<p>Loops are used to execute the same block of code a specified number of times.</p>\n<h4>For Loop:</h4>\n<pre><code class=\"language-php\">&lt;?php\n  for ($i = 1; $i &lt;= 5; $i++) {\n    echo \"The number is: $i &lt;br&gt;\";\n  }\n?&gt;</code></pre>\n<h4>While Loop:</h4>\n<pre><code class=\"language-php\">&lt;?php\n  $count = 5;\n\n  while($count &lt;= 15) {\n    echo $count;\n    echo \"&lt;br&gt;\" ;\n    $count++;\n  }\n?&gt;</code></pre>\n<h3>Functions</h3>\n<p>Functions are blocks of code that can be reused in a program.</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-php\">&lt;?php\n  function add($x, $y) {\n    return $x + $y;\n  }\n\n  echo \"5 + 10 = \" . add(5, 10);\n?&gt;</code></pre>\n<h3>Arrays</h3>\n<p>Arrays are used to store multiple values in a single variable.</p>\n<h4>Indexed Array:</h4>\n<pre><code class=\"language-php\">&lt;?php\n  $cars = array(\"Volvo\", \"BMW\", \"Toyota\");\n  echo \"I like \" . $cars[0] . \", \" . $cars[1] . \" and \" . $cars[2] . \".\";\n?&gt;</code></pre>\n<h4>Associative Array:</h4>\n<pre><code class=\"language-php\">&lt;?php\n  $person = array(\"name\" =&gt; \"John\", \"age\" =&gt; 25, \"gender\" =&gt; \"Male\");\n  echo \"Name: \" . $person[\"name\"] . \"&lt;br&gt;\";\n  echo \"Age: \" . $person[\"age\"] . \"&lt;br&gt;\";\n  echo \"Gender: \" . $person[\"gender\"];\n?&gt;</code></pre>\n<h3>Form Handling</h3>\n<p>PHP is often used to process form data. Here\'s a simple example of how to handle a form submission.</p>\n<p><strong>HTML Form (<code>index.html</code>):</strong></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-html\">&lt;form action=\"welcome.php\" method=\"post\"&gt;\n  Name: &lt;input type=\"text\" name=\"name\"&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n  E-mail: &lt;input type=\"text\" name=\"email\"&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n  &lt;input type=\"submit\"&gt;\n&lt;/form&gt;</code></pre>\n<p><strong>PHP Script (<code>welcome.php</code>):</strong></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-php\">&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n\nWelcome &lt;?php echo $_POST[\"name\"]; ?&gt;&lt;br&gt;\nYour email address is: &lt;?php echo $_POST[\"email\"]; ?&gt;\n\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;</code></pre>\n<h3>Simple To-Do List</h3>\n<p>For a more complete and practical example, you can find the source code for a simple to-do list application which includes features like adding, editing, deleting, and marking tasks as complete. This type of project typically involves connecting to a MySQL database to store and retrieve task information.</p>\";raw_result|s:2679:\"Of course, here are some PHP code samples ranging from basic to more advanced examples.\n\n### Basic \"Hello, World!\"\n\nThis is a classic example to demonstrate the basic syntax of PHP. It uses the `echo` statement to display a string of text.\n\n```php\n<?php\n  echo \"Hello, World!\";\n?>\n```\n\n### Variables\n\nVariables are used to store information. In PHP, a variable starts with a `$` sign, followed by the name of the variable.\n\n```php\n<?php\n  $greeting = \"Hello!\";\n  $month = 8;\n  $year = 2019;\n\n  echo $greeting; // Outputs: Hello!\n  echo $month;   // Outputs: 8\n  echo $year;    // Outputs: 2019\n?>\n```\n\n### Conditional Statements (if-else)\n\nConditional statements are used to perform different actions based on different conditions.\n\n```php\n<?php\n  $age = 20;\n\n  if ($age >= 18) {\n    echo \"You are an adult.\";\n  } else {\n    echo \"You are a minor.\";\n  }\n?>\n```\n\n### Loops\n\nLoops are used to execute the same block of code a specified number of times.\n\n#### For Loop:\n\n```php\n<?php\n  for ($i = 1; $i <= 5; $i++) {\n    echo \"The number is: $i <br>\";\n  }\n?>\n```\n\n#### While Loop:\n\n```php\n<?php\n  $count = 5;\n\n  while($count <= 15) {\n    echo $count;\n    echo \"<br>\" ;\n    $count++;\n  }\n?>\n```\n\n### Functions\n\nFunctions are blocks of code that can be reused in a program.\n\n```php\n<?php\n  function add($x, $y) {\n    return $x + $y;\n  }\n\n  echo \"5 + 10 = \" . add(5, 10);\n?>\n```\n\n### Arrays\n\nArrays are used to store multiple values in a single variable.\n\n#### Indexed Array:\n\n```php\n<?php\n  $cars = array(\"Volvo\", \"BMW\", \"Toyota\");\n  echo \"I like \" . $cars[0] . \", \" . $cars[1] . \" and \" . $cars[2] . \".\";\n?>\n```\n\n#### Associative Array:\n\n```php\n<?php\n  $person = array(\"name\" => \"John\", \"age\" => 25, \"gender\" => \"Male\");\n  echo \"Name: \" . $person[\"name\"] . \"<br>\";\n  echo \"Age: \" . $person[\"age\"] . \"<br>\";\n  echo \"Gender: \" . $person[\"gender\"];\n?>\n```\n\n### Form Handling\n\nPHP is often used to process form data. Here\'s a simple example of how to handle a form submission.\n\n**HTML Form (`index.html`):**\n\n```html\n<form action=\"welcome.php\" method=\"post\">\n  Name: <input type=\"text\" name=\"name\"><br>\n  E-mail: <input type=\"text\" name=\"email\"><br>\n  <input type=\"submit\">\n</form>\n```\n\n**PHP Script (`welcome.php`):**\n\n```php\n<html>\n<body>\n\nWelcome <?php echo $_POST[\"name\"]; ?><br>\nYour email address is: <?php echo $_POST[\"email\"]; ?>\n\n</body>\n</html>\n```\n\n### Simple To-Do List\n\nFor a more complete and practical example, you can find the source code for a simple to-do list application which includes features like adding, editing, deleting, and marking tasks as complete. This type of project typically involves connecting to a MySQL database to store and retrieve task information.\";'),('ci_session:f6a9a6234a0f88c81c32b652c7804562','::1',4294967295,_binary '__ci_last_regenerate|i:1764234844;_ci_previous_url|s:24:\"https://localhost/ollama\";isLoggedIn|b:1;userId|i:1;userEmail|s:23:\"nehemiahobati@gmail.com\";username|s:8:\"nehemiah\";is_admin|b:1;member_since|O:21:\"CodeIgniter\\I18n\\Time\":6:{s:4:\"date\";s:26:\"2025-11-20 22:30:57.000000\";s:13:\"timezone_type\";i:3;s:8:\"timezone\";s:14:\"Africa/Nairobi\";s:11:\"\0*\0timezone\";O:12:\"DateTimeZone\":2:{s:13:\"timezone_type\";i:3;s:8:\"timezone\";s:14:\"Africa/Nairobi\";}s:9:\"\0*\0locale\";s:2:\"en\";s:17:\"\0*\0toStringFormat\";s:19:\"yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss\";}_ci_old_input|a:2:{s:3:\"get\";a:0:{}s:4:\"post\";a:3:{s:6:\"prompt\";s:15:\"<p>summerry</p>\";s:14:\"uploaded_media\";a:1:{i:0;s:36:\"1764231919_ee29a06b664d2f6df900.jpeg\";}s:5:\"model\";s:37:\"hf.co/LiquidAI/LFM2-VL-450M-GGUF:Q4_0\";}}__ci_vars|a:4:{s:13:\"_ci_old_input\";s:3:\"old\";s:6:\"result\";s:3:\"old\";s:10:\"raw_result\";s:3:\"old\";s:7:\"success\";s:3:\"old\";}result|s:2089:\"<p>The image shows a page from a newspaper. The page contains text and sections, with one of the headlines reading &quot;Ex-AG Wars Claims Fund Illegal.&quot; Below the headline are two paragraphs of text providing information or context about the news story. The first paragraph discusses how &quot;Justin Muturi,&quot; the Governor, has decided to set aside claims of legal infighting within the Ministry of Public Service under a new body established by the Legislature. The second paragraph provides further details on how this body was formed and its functions.</p>\n<p>The page also includes several numbered sections, labeled 1 through 10, each with headings that provide additional information about these topics. These sections are organized in a grid-like pattern across the page, suggesting a systematic layout intended for easy navigation by the reader.</p>\n<p>There is also a photo of an elderly man, presumably a significant figure related to the story, which adds a visual element to the text narrative. The presence of a photograph might indicate that the individual has a personal connection to the topic or the government, adding credibility and a human touch to the information presented on the page.</p>\n<p>The newspaper page is neatly organized with sections for different topics, each with headings that are clear and easy to read. The use of bold text for the headline &quot;Ex-AG Wars Claims Fund Illegal&quot; draws attention to the central topic of the article. The section below it provides detailed information on the actions taken by the Governor under this decision, including the establishment of a new body tasked with overseeing such claims and the legal framework governing these situations.</p>\n<p>Overall, the page is well-structured and informative, presenting a clear and concise narrative about the government\'s decision to disengage from certain legal claims under a specific program or legislation. The inclusion of visual elements like the photo and the structured text sections further enhances the readability and engagement with the content.</p>\";raw_result|s:2028:\"The image shows a page from a newspaper. The page contains text and sections, with one of the headlines reading \"Ex-AG Wars Claims Fund Ill